Hmm.. ok... since there's been a bit of talk about common causes of
death, and how well one tends to do on average...
I looked at the records file for my game, to see how I was doing
in this regards...
I'm on a unix based machine, and am the only one who plays it, so all
games were mine, and at most 3 of each class will be written into the
records file for a particular username, so we have my top 3 games playing
each class. (granted I have not played 3 games with a few of them)

class     num entries   result (and where)

Archaeologist 3  ascended, giant spider (mines12), killer bee poison (mines6) 
Barbarian     1  drowned in moat by kraken (51)
Caveman       3  poisoned by Juiblex (35), dwarf (mines6), Mordor orc (mines4)
Elf           3  owlbear (mines8), owlbear (mines6), priestess (mines5)
Healer        3  iguana (4), dwarf (6), hill orc (4)
Knight        3  ascended, dwarf (mines7), gnome king (mines8)
Priest        2  plains centaur (4), giant rat (3)
Rogue         3  plains centaur (4), fire ant (mines5), acidic corpse (4)
Samarai       1  elf-lord (14)
Tourist       3  invis. stalker (9), shopkeeper (mines6), shopkeeper (mines6)
Valkyrie      3  leocrotta (9), troll (7), invis. stalker (mines10)
Wizard        3  wolf (4), angry god (4), hobgoblin (4)

So, owlbears, plains centaurs, invisible stalkers, shopkeepers and
dwarfs are all tied with two kills apiece. =)
The angry god death and acidic corpse death were suicides.

'Tis interesting to note that of the 31 games (2 of which were
ascensions, so only 29 deaths) 13 of them died in the mines.
9 died before reaching the mines. 1 never found the mines at all. =)
Of the 8 that made it out of the mines, 4 made it to the quest.
Of those 4, 2 ascended.
So, if you can survive the mines, things tend to look up from there. =)
All of these results are with no spoiler info. And only a good knowledge
of 3.0 to work from (figuring out the bell/candelabrum/book thing is
a MAJOR pain with no hints)

Note: this is playing some of the more dificult classes too.
      I'm sure if I'd played barbarians or samarais more then once, (or
